    "updated_at": "2024-03-13T19:38:18Z",
    "body": "yeah, I encounter the similar issue on Ubuntu 20.04 that claim the interface automatically. I used a simple script in python to detach the kernel driver. I think the reason they don't implement that feature is because it is different for different platforms and it touches a lot of low-level stuff for different platform, not sure if there is a general fix for that. I can confirm that you don't face the same issue on MacOS not sure on Windows. \r\nDo you have any idea on how to solve the issue without touch the `udev` or running the python script like I did for linux? \r\nI'm developing a tool to send usb data to the device for end users and I don't want them to go down to the low level such as that\r\n",
