    "created_at": "2025-05-23T12:02:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-23T12:02:49Z",
    "body": "Regarding [Chromium issue 40137537](https://crbug.com/40137537): this feature was implemented and is being launched for Chromium on Android with the hardcoded allowlist of USB drivers that can be detached: `usblp`, `ftdi_sio` and `cdc_acm`. The `cdc_acm` driver provides interfaces of two classes: `Communications` and `CDC Data`, but the allowlist only contains interfaces of `Communications` class with AT-command sets or without any protocol set.\n\n_Note_: If you need to claim the `CDC Data` interface, you have to claim its control interface first, this will detach the `cdc_acm` driver, and then you will be able to claim the `CDC Data` interface.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
